---
term: Constitutional feedback loop
section: accountability
order: 30
definition: The cycle through which a charter learns from results and revises its objectives or rules.
seeAlso:
  - measurement-mechanism
  - amendment
  - audit
---
1. Define an objective.
1. Take action.
1. Measure results.
1. Evaluate performance.
1. Detect failures.
1. Amend the objective or rules.
1. Repeat.

This loop makes the constitution an adaptive control system instead of a static legal text. A bad policy doesn't mean the constitution has failed. The charter can learn and evolve.
